       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for ibuprofen in adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. The OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg at once is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- **Risks:** At this dose the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up sharply. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't offset that.\n\n**Possible intended orders:**\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day total)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day), which is a common maximum for inflammatory conditions\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), which is the absolute ceiling\n\n1600 mg may have been meant as the total daily dose. If so, 400 mg four times daily would match it.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm the indication if you mean something different, and I'll enter it right away."
